  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The town of Hyères created a dog beach on Mérou beach, at L'Ayguade, between L'Ayguade and Les Salins: a seaside area for dogs where owners can walk their dog and let it enjoy a swim. The area is marked off by ganivelle fencing carrying clear signage for owners. According to Nice-Matin, it came out of a petition with more than 25,000 signatures and covers a strip about a hundred metres long. The Provence Méditerranée tourist office states it is open all year, every day.</p>

      <h2>The rule for dogs</h2>
      <p>Municipal order no. 2026-1420 of 16 July 2026 (article 11) bans dogs from the town's beaches, except guide dogs and beach areas specifically authorised by order, "notably Mérou beach": so stay within the designated area. Visit Var specifies that the beach is open to dogs on a leash, with a shaded area of umbrella pines, a few tables and enough room to run your dog or picnic. On the Vieux Salins coastal path and on the salt road when it is closed to traffic, dogs must be on a leash.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: elsewhere in Hyères, don't assume a beach is open to dogs; the 2026 order bans them outside expressly authorised areas.</div>

      <h2>Cleanliness and facilities</h2>
      <p>The town asks visitors to pick up droppings and put them in the bins provided; bag dispensers are available near the beach entrances, and Visit Var mentions bins in the car park. According to the town, there is no beach shower in 2026 because of water restrictions: bring fresh water to rinse your dog after the swim.</p>

      <h2>Shared with kitesurfing</h2>
      <p>The same order designates Mérou beach, along with L'Almanarre, as an authorised launch and landing area for kitesurfing within the 300-metre strip. Keep your dog close when kitesurfers are preparing their gear.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/en/fiche-le-pradet-caniplouf">Cani Plouf in Le Pradet</a>, to the west, is another dog beach in the area.</p>
    </div>

